From: violetc <58360096+s-yh-china@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Feb 2024 19:50:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix falling block's block location

Ported from LeavesMC/Leaves master (0093-Fix-falling-block-s-block-location.patch), GPL-3.0-only.
Original author: violetc.
Canvas adaptation: local variable names adapted to our setPos implementation (fx/fy/fz instead of floor/floor1/floor2); insertion point moved after our Folia posChanged guard, behavior identical

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index 081f39ee72f48ae9951d54574e8acba6e8549942..4d09592fa88ca5fb5d4ae545ec4a94e89b84006c 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -6562,6 +6562,15 @@ public abstract class Entity
             int fx = Mth.floor(x);
             int fy = Mth.floor(y);
             int fz = Mth.floor(z);
+
+            // Leaves start - fix falling block location
+            if (this instanceof net.minecraft.world.entity.item.FallingBlockEntity) {
+                if (y < 0.0 && y + 1e-10 > 0.0) {
+                    fy = 0;
+                }
+            }
+            // Leaves end - fix falling block location
+
             if (fx != this.blockPosition.getX() || fy != this.blockPosition.getY() || fz != this.blockPosition.getZ()) {
                 this.blockPosition = new BlockPos(fx, fy, fz);
                 this.inBlockState = null;
